# Ownership for the paths that decide what CI runs.
#
# `scripts/ci/rust-scope.sh` is the whitelist that lets a pull request skip the required Rust checks,
# and `.github/workflows/` and `.github/actions/` are those checks. The workflow already refuses to
# skip a change set that touches them, and it classifies with the *base* revision's copy so a pull
# request cannot rewrite the rule to excuse itself. This is the human half: a whitelist widened for
# the wrong reason looks exactly like one widened for the right one in the diff.
#
# The repo ruleset has `require_code_owner_review` off, so these entries request a review from the
# owner of a touched path rather than block a merge on it. That is the intent: visibility on CI
# changes, not a second gate on top of the one CI already enforces.
# See docs/decisions/2026-10-18-rust-ci-skips-prose-only-changes.md.
/scripts/ci/        @CypherNaught-0x
/.github/workflows/ @CypherNaught-0x
/.github/actions/   @CypherNaught-0x
